Fixed #1234 and committed. When stdout can't be written (for example a full disk), yoyo -p now prints one stderr line, error writing to stdout: No space left on device (os error 28), and exits 1. That holds in text, --print, json and stream-json. Build, the full cargo test, clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check all pass.

Before and after (built binary, stdout sent to /dev/full, a local 127.0.0.1 server standing in for the API):

| format | before | after |
|---|---|---|
| text -p | exit 0, nothing on stderr | exit 1, one error line |
| --print | exit 0, nothing on stderr | exit 1, one error line |
| json | exit 101 (panic) | exit 1, one error line |
| stream-json | exit 0, nothing on stderr | exit 1, one error line |

The two near-miss cases behave as they did before the change. A normal run to a pipe exits 0 with the answer and no error line. A pipe whose reader has already closed still dies quietly by SIGPIPE (signal 13), with no error line and no panic. I didn't touch the SIGPIPE setting in main.rs, and a broken-pipe error is never reported.

How it works: a new src/stdout_write.rs records the first stdout write error that isn't a broken pipe. Everything that writes the answer now hands its result to it instead of dropping it or panicking:
• streamed text and the other text on stdout (prompt.rs)
• --print and the json output (main.rs)
• each stream-json line, which also stops writing once stdout has failed

The four exit paths for -p and piped input flush stdout, print the error line and turn exit 0 into 1. A run that was already failing keeps its own non-zero code.

Checks:
• New test: tests/stdout_write_failure.rs has 6 tests (Linux only, since it needs /dev/full): one per format on a full disk, plus the two near-miss cases.
• Recall control: I disabled the exit-code branch with a marker (count 1 confirmed before the run). The four full-disk tests failed by name and the near-miss tests stayed green. After restoring it (marker count 0), all 6 passed.
• Lock gate: an existing repo test caught my first draft copying lock-recovery code. It now uses sync_util::lock_or_recover.
• On the issue: I posted the before-table on #1234 before editing any code, and the after-table plus control result before the full test run.

Outside the plan:
• The plan allowed main.rs, one new test file and one more source file. I also edited prompt.rs and two modules under src/prompt/, because that's where the writers are. prompt.rs stays the same length.
• Runs that already fail with exit 1 for another reason (an API error, a bad image) still don't print the stdout error line.
• I added one paragraph to the exit-codes section of docs/src/usage/single-prompt.md.

All four formats are covered, so the commit says Fixes #1234.

